1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:02,669
♪

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:04,087
[NARRATOR] At long last,

3
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:06,548
the civil war
tearing Missian apart

4
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:08,550
came to an end when Lord Couran

5
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:11,637
had his younger brother,
Vasmarque, executed.

6
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:15,933
In winning the battle
against the invading Seitz army

7
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,101
and its vaunted commander,
Borotz,

8
00:00:18,185 --> 00:00:21,021
Ars and his comrades
grew even stronger.

9
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,690
Hoping to secure
a more lasting peace,

10
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:27,027
Ars has decided he will pursue
the path of emperor.

11
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:31,531
However,
the protracted and brutal war

12
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,993
has left innumerable deep scars
on Canarre.

13
00:00:38,664 --> 00:00:40,582
[♪ opening theme song playing]

14
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:14,760
Hey, Lord Ars.

15
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,179
Uh, Rietz,
do you know where he is?

16
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,723
Seems he had to travel
to the estate in Lamberg

17
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:22,059
for a meeting with someone
on rather short notice.

18
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:24,686
Oh? Well, I'm sorry
I missed him.

19
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,575
[ARS] So, what does
that machine do?

20
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:39,701
[SHIN] Hm?

21
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,954
Well, what do you know?
It's the little man.

22
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:44,748
Didn't expect to see you today.

23
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:47,042
I'm so happy
you got that nice, fat payout

24
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,210
for winning the war.

25
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,379
We can make so much more
with that kind of budget!

26
00:02:50,462 --> 00:02:52,047
Though my schedule
will be packed

27
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,340
with all the stuff I wanna do!

28
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:54,925
That's great to hear.

29
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:57,511
At this point, I don't think
it'll actually be too long

30
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:58,637
before I can make you

31
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,347
a giant,
fully functional airship.

32
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,516
You're an amazing inventor,
Shin.

33
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:05,268
And your technology was crucial
in winning the war.

34
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:08,397
Canarre is peaceful once again,
thanks to you.

35
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,024
I really appreciate you
putting in all that hard work

36
00:03:11,108 --> 00:03:13,110
to get it operational
so quickly.

37
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:16,405
No sweat. But I guess
I did kinda save the day, huh?

38
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:17,614
You did!

39
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:20,826
I'd like to apologize to you
for something.

40
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,702
Not long after we first met,

41
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:24,913
I asked you if you would
become my retainer,

42
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:26,373
which is a big commitment.

43
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:29,918
But after this war,
I've had a realization.

44
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,797
Your inventions will surely make
so many new things possible.

45
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,841
That's true
not only in day-to-day life,

46
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,634
but on the battlefield as well.

47
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:40,470
So I realize that I shouldn't be
treating you as a retainer,

48
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:42,013
but rather as an equal.

49
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,058
I know of a place far away

50
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:47,811
where their inability
to rein in technology

51
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,188
caused unspeakable tragedy.

52
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,316
You could have
the most incredible creations.

53
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,318
But if a leader chose
to misuse them,

54
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:57,612
it could lead
to dire consequences.

55
00:03:57,696 --> 00:03:59,739
Widespread death
and destruction.

56
00:04:00,282 --> 00:04:03,160
So if you think I've asked you
to make something dangerous,

57
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,536
don't do it.

58
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:06,746
If you think
my intentions are malicious,

59
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:07,956
you can leave.

60
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:10,625
If that does happen,

61
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:14,296
then it means I'm truly unworthy
of your incredible technology.

62
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,631
Ultimately, I would be the one
who's responsible

63
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:19,426
for how your creations
would be utilized.

64
00:04:20,552 --> 00:04:22,679
Long ago, father told me...

65
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:25,348
"Find the face of a warrior."

66
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,937
And the way I understood it
back then,

67
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,397
I thought that he meant
I should prepare

68
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:34,399
to not only see
lives taken in battle,

69
00:04:34,483 --> 00:04:36,151
but to take them myself.

70
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:38,528
Of course,
that was only one part of it.

71
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:41,490
But it was far more complicated
than just that.

72
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,117
Because truly becoming a warrior

73
00:04:44,201 --> 00:04:47,204
means taking full responsibility
for your actions.

74
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,457
Holding yourself accountable
for everything you do,

75
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,750
good and bad.

76
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:54,669
Ultimate responsibility,

77
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:57,339
it's weightier and sometimes
even more painful

78
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:59,549
than the life-or-death
of the battlefield.

79
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:01,468
But it is my sworn duty
as a lord

80
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:02,928
to shoulder that burden.

81
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:04,930
For the sake of my people,

82
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,806
I have the responsibility
to ensure

83
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:09,226
that the future we create
is a peaceful one.

84
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,852
So now, tell me, Shin,

85
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:12,729
do you think
that you're prepared

86
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:15,398
to take on that burden
alongside of me?

87
00:05:16,358 --> 00:05:17,526
[Shin sighs]

88
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:22,697
One question. You're giving me
all these resources to create

89
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:26,284
and taking ownership
of whatever happens next. Why?

90
00:05:26,368 --> 00:05:29,204
I wholeheartedly believe
that your creations

91
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,956
will bring about
the kind of changes

92
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,999
that will make
people's lives better.

93
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,377
[SHIN] But what if I fail?

94
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,920
[ARS] Well, that may happen.

95
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:39,756
But I'm sure nobody understands
better than you...

96
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:42,884
That there's no such thing
as success without failure.

97
00:05:43,385 --> 00:05:44,844
[Shin gasps softly]

98
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:49,057
You've always been on my side,
and I couldn't ask

99
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,226
for a more supportive little guy
than you.

100
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,772
Yeah! This means I never have
to give up on my dream!

101
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:58,733
I'll make an airship big enough
for people, and when I do,

102
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:01,027
you're gonna be the first one
to go for a ride!

103
00:06:01,111 --> 00:06:02,863
Wow! That's so exciting!

104
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:06,825
Check this out, little man.
I was working on a way

105
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:09,327
to give these airships of ours
some more firepower,

106
00:06:09,411 --> 00:06:10,954
and I stumbled onto something.

107
00:06:11,413 --> 00:06:13,456
When you mix
these two chemicals together,

108
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:15,250
it'll blow up like crazy.

109
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,085
[ARS] Hold on. Wait, Shin!

110
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:23,300
[clattering]

111
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:25,635
[Ars grunts softly]

112
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:27,304
[gasps softly]

113
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,307
See what I mean?

114
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,642
This stuff is gonna make
excavating magistones

115
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:33,977
so much easier!

116
00:06:35,979 --> 00:06:37,564
[hooves clopping]

117
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:45,488
[horse neighs]

118
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:48,575
[SOLDIER 1] Looks like someone
was making camp here.

119
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:49,659
This is gotta be

120
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,995
where those damn bandits
have been staying.

121
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:55,624
[indistinct chatter]

122
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:59,628
We need to track them all down
and bring them in.

123
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:01,254
Some raggedy bunch of bandits

124
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:03,214
are nothing against
the Canarre Army!

125
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:05,133
-[SOLDIERS] Yes, sir!
-[footsteps]

126
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:07,302
[gasps] Is someone there?
[grunts]

127
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:10,263
Hey! Let's take these bastards
down now!

128
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,766
Wait, what in the hell
is going on here?

129
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:13,933
Where are they coming from?

130
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:16,144
Do you have a visual on them
or what?

131
00:07:16,603 --> 00:07:18,355
[SOLDIER 2]
No, I can't see anyone.

132
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,857
[SOLDIER 1] What do you mean
you can't see them?

133
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,317
[SOLDIER 2]
I think they're invisible.

134
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,318
[grunting]

135
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:24,944
-[neighs]
-[soldier screams]

136
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:26,196
[grunting]

137
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,495
♪

138
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:49,094
Hey, Rietz! I just got back.

139
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,846
Lord Ars, I'm glad you're home.

140
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:53,848
Unfortunately,
there's a troubling situation

141
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:55,767
that's come up
since you've been gone.

142
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:56,976
[ARS] Hmm?

143
00:07:58,478 --> 00:07:59,813
Bandits?

144
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,315
They just attacked a fort
that we were defending

145
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,150
without any kind of warning.

146
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,319
We sent out a regiment
to search the nearby mountains

147
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:07,445
for any sign of them,

148
00:08:07,821 --> 00:08:09,614
and the very moment
that we discovered the area

149
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:11,241
where they'd been
making their camp,

150
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,118
they quickly overwhelmed
our men.

151
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:14,953
The strange thing was
we couldn't see them,

152
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:17,539
just heard some footsteps,
and then we were out cold.

153
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,457
So you never caught a glimpse
of them?

154
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:21,626
No. Like I'd said,
we heard someone moving,

155
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:22,794
but when we looked around,

156
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,713
we couldn't see anyone
approaching us.

157
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,132
I'm afraid this means

158
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:29,217
that the bandits
must still be at large.

159
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:32,011
Well, if these bandits
have some kind of invisibility,

160
00:08:32,095 --> 00:08:33,972
does that mean
they're able to use shade magic

161
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,974
-like Pham and his Shadow guys?
-Huh.

162
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:38,017
Maybe just a hunch on my part,

163
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:40,729
but this feels like something
other than magic to me.

164
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,273
I've heard rumors
that they've been operating

165
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:45,400
from an abandoned castle
on the border.

166
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:47,819
We need to find a way
to deal with them quickly.

167
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:50,029
Is Rosell around?

168
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:51,990
He's out
on a diplomatic mission.

169
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:54,034
I'd like to pick his brain.

170
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:55,952
Well, in any case,

171
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:58,413
let's handle it
before they strike again.

172
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:00,623
[MAN 1]
They've gotta be the bandits

173
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:01,833
everyone's talking about.

174
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,794
[MAN 2] They're definitely
not from around here.

175
00:09:04,878 --> 00:09:06,296
Did you not hear me?

176
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:08,673
We are not the foul bandits
of which you speak.

177
00:09:08,757 --> 00:09:10,592
How many times
must I repeat myself?

178
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:13,678
Yeah? You wanna explain
those weird outfits you've got?

179
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:15,638
You look very suspicious to me.

180
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:18,141
What's more, that sword
your friend's got on him

181
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,894
is obviously
extremely expensive.

182
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,187
If you want me to believe

183
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,480
you're not
with that bandit group,

184
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:24,898
you're gonna have
to prove it to me.

185
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,316
-[snores]
-[MAIKA] How would I do that?

186
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:29,277
Then you're coming with us,
do you hear? [grunts]

187
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,237
Halt! Hands off, you damn fool!

188
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:33,573
Well, now
I'm even more suspicious.

189
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:35,116
You really are the bandits,

190
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,326
-aren't you?
-[grunting]

191
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:38,953
Will somebody please tell me
what all this commotion's about?

192
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:41,206
[GUARD] Oh, Lord Ars.

193
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:43,917
Are you here because you wish
to apprehend us as well?

194
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,001
[ARS] Huh?

195
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:48,880
No matter then, we will fight
for our sovereignty.

196
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,673
Takao, get up!

197
00:09:50,757 --> 00:09:52,884
And dispense
with these brutes post haste!

198
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:53,885
[Takao grunts]

199
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:58,515
[grunting]

200
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,982
[RIETZ] How is he able
to move like that?

201
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:09,651
I've never seen
anything like it.

202
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:10,902
Rietz, no!

203
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,532
Calm down.
What's wrong with you?

204
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:16,825
[TAKAO] Huh?

205
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:18,952
Honestly, you're far too quick
to violence.

206
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,161
[Ars gasps]

207
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:23,790
Right. Please forgive me,
elder brother.

208
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:27,293
Same goes for you, Maika.
You need to apologize.

209
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:30,547
But why? I seriously believe
they would attack us.

210
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,549
♪

211
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,845
I humbly ask forgiveness.

212
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:39,556
Yes, of course. It's all right.

213
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:46,563
[ARS] Those clothes definitely
aren't from Missian.

214
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:49,023
If you folks
don't mind me asking,

215
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,316
can you tell us who you are?

216
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,906
We are merely simple travelers

217
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,742
who've only arrived
in your land a few days ago.

218
00:10:59,826 --> 00:11:02,161
Seems the unfamiliarity
has us on edge.

219
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:03,329
I beg your pardon.

220
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:05,456
Uh? From what I've gathered,

221
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:08,334
the bandits have been at large
for at least a month, correct?

222
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:09,919
I don't believe
these people here

223
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:12,130
have anything to do
with all that.

224
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:14,215
Yes, my lord.
I'll take your word for it.

225
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:20,722
[ARS]
Her Ingenuity stat is high,

226
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,807
and she's an S-rank strategist.

227
00:11:22,891 --> 00:11:25,143
It's like she was born
to lead an army!

228
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,854
And he's got incredible Prowess!

229
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:31,649
High infantry, cavalry,
and archery affinities as well!

230
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:34,193
I bet he's undefeated
on the battlefield!

231
00:11:34,277 --> 00:11:36,654
They're practically
polar opposites,

232
00:11:36,738 --> 00:11:38,197
but both of them
are extraordinary

233
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:40,158
in their respective abilities.

234
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,619
Wonder what he's got going on.

235
00:11:43,745 --> 00:11:45,872
All his stats
are above average, too!

236
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,624
The guy's
a well-balanced all-rounder

237
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,417
who can do about anything!

238
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:52,170
What I wouldn't give

239
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,797
to have these three powerhouses
on my side!

240
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:56,090
[gasps]

241
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:59,177
Looks like all three of them
have the same family name.

242
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,887
Are they siblings?

243
00:12:01,221 --> 00:12:03,389
And they were all born
in the Kingdom of Yoh,

244
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:05,016
the next continent over.

245
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:08,061
Is that why their outfits have
a kind of oriental feel to them?

246
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,188
So, um... I, uh...

247
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:12,732
[RIKUYA] We're terribly sorry
for the disturbance.

248
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:15,026
All right, you two,
we should be going now.

249
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:16,236
Hold on just one second.

250
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,488
I don't believe that
I caught your name, my friend.

251
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,239
It's not important,
I assure you.

252
00:12:20,323 --> 00:12:22,200
As I said,
we're just ordinary travelers.

253
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,661
Well, do you think
you could stay another moment

254
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,037
and speak with me?

255
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,373
-Wait! Come back, please!
-[RIKUYA] Leave us be!

256
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:35,004
[RIKUYA] So you're the lord
of this land, are you?

257
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:37,090
Yes, that's me.

258
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:40,760
His name is Ars Louvent,
headman of the Canarre district.

259
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,097
First let me say,

260
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:45,932
I would like
to formally apologize

261
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,392
for what happened earlier.

262
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:48,851
This rash of bandit attacks

263
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:50,853
has had everybody
on pins and needles.

264
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:53,940
I understand.
Is that why you were there?

265
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:55,608
[RIETZ] Before we go further,

266
00:12:55,692 --> 00:12:57,402
there's something
I'd like to know.

267
00:12:57,485 --> 00:13:00,071
I'm curious as to why
the royal family

268
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:01,739
would be traveling abroad
without a guard.

269
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:03,408
[all grunt softly]

270
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,118
"Royal family"?

271
00:13:05,994 --> 00:13:07,287
[both exhale]

272
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:13,126
What makes you think
that's who we are?

273
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,336
The sword you're wearing

274
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,130
has rather distinct
ornamentation.

275
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:20,341
If I'm not mistaken,
they're rare blue diamonds.

276
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:24,846
Those blue diamonds
carry a special significance.

277
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:27,974
Only members of the royal family
of the Yoh Kingdom

278
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,475
are permitted to wear them.

279
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:32,645
And by carrying them
on you like that,

280
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:34,647
it indicates
that you're a royal.

281
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,651
What business would
Yoh's royal family

282
00:13:38,735 --> 00:13:40,028
have here in Canarre?

283
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:41,237
♪

284
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:46,492
It's as you say.

285
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,163
This sword I hold...

286
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,498
it is a legacy
of House Fujimiya.

287
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,460
The Dragonslayer.

288
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:57,670
The legends sing
of how it was used

289
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:58,921
to strike down a dragon.

290
00:13:59,005 --> 00:14:00,757
That can slay a dragon?

291
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,675
Elder brother!

292
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:05,178
[RIKUYA] Calm yourself.
Clearly, we can't hide it.

293
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:10,266
Forgive me for saying that
we were "ordinary travelers."

294
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:12,518
The truth is

295
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,771
that I am the current head
of House Fujimiya

296
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,565
and the king of Yoh,
Rikuya Fujimiya.

297
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:19,692
What? You say
you're the king of Yoh?

298
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:21,819
I mean, that's basically
like being the emperor

299
00:14:21,903 --> 00:14:23,196
of another continent!

300
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:26,157
What's someone of your status
doing in a random Canarre inn?

301
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,704
It's because
of last year's uprising.

302
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,706
[both breathe uneasily]

303
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:35,458
An uprising?

304
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,544
[RIETZ] Yes. I'd heard there was
a rebellion in Yoh

305
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:40,797
and the royal family
had been overthrown.

306
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:44,092
But still, I didn't realize
there were survivors.

307
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,594
[RIKUYA] Once cast out of Yoh,

308
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:48,846
we then traveled here
to Summerforth.

309
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:51,933
Our one goal
is finding someone to help.

310
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,851
We wish to return
to our homeland

311
00:14:53,935 --> 00:14:56,104
so we can retake the throne.

312
00:14:56,187 --> 00:14:59,649
Alas, even our former allies
turned us away.

313
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,234
But we're holding onto hope.

314
00:15:01,317 --> 00:15:03,027
[grunts]
Listen, we'd be on our way

315
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:04,987
if you would take my advice
to sell that sword

316
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,280
and get us some money.

317
00:15:06,364 --> 00:15:08,032
Our war is
practically a lost cause,

318
00:15:08,116 --> 00:15:10,451
so nobody
will help us out for free.

319
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:11,828
We're very close

320
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:14,122
to running out of
what little money we have.

321
00:15:14,205 --> 00:15:15,373
If nothing changes,

322
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:17,458
we'll have to do
what we must to survive.

323
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:20,086
Sorry, I know.

324
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:23,714
But this blade,
it marks me as the king of Yoh.

325
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:27,468
If I don't have it,
I cannot prove my royal lineage.

326
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:30,012
Well, what purpose
does it even serve

327
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,597
if we're unable to return home?

328
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:37,520
[RIKUYA]
In any case, that's our story.

329
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,522
It's likely that
assassins have been sent

330
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,023
to take our heads,

331
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:43,943
so we must be cautious
when revealing our identities.

332
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:48,030
Yes, I understand.
It's such a terrible situation.

333
00:15:48,114 --> 00:15:51,200
My condolences for everything
that you've had to endure.

334
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:53,619
[RIKUYA]
It's nothing. We'll manage.

335
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:55,663
[sighs]

336
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,040
And forgive my asking,

337
00:15:58,124 --> 00:15:59,750
but since you are the lord here,

338
00:15:59,834 --> 00:16:02,211
could you introduce us
to your governor?

339
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:03,921
Given our circumstance,

340
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:06,507
I fear we'll need assistance
to secure his aid.

341
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:08,384
Oh, yes, of course!

342
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:10,052
Our meeting was destiny.

343
00:16:10,136 --> 00:16:13,139
We'll be happy to help you
in any way we possibly can.

344
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,765
-[stomach growling]
-Huh?

345
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,810
Elder brother,
I'm getting hungry.

346
00:16:17,894 --> 00:16:19,645
-[Maika's stomach growling]
-[BOTH] Huh?

347
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:21,981
I am as well, elder brother.

348
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:24,817
Our diet has been very meager
these past several days.

349
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,403
Oh, no. Then please,
come to Canarre!

350
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:30,156
We would love for you to join us
for dinner tonight.

351
00:16:30,865 --> 00:16:33,409
Yes, we would
greatly appreciate it.

352
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:35,036
[insects trilling]

353
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:41,167
[footsteps]

354
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,712
-[thumping]
-[grunting]

355
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,505
[footsteps]

356
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,721
Ooh, it has been so long
since we've had a feast.

357
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:54,972
I'm so happy.

358
00:16:55,056 --> 00:16:57,308
You sure we can eat
as much as we want?

359
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:59,227
You heard the lord invite us,
didn't you?

360
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:01,103
Do you think
they would deny you sustenance?

361
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:03,147
Clearly,
he's a rather generous fellow!

362
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:04,565
You're right. I can see that.

363
00:17:04,649 --> 00:17:06,943
And you're certain
that we're not imposing?

364
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,694
Not at all.
I welcome your company,

365
00:17:08,778 --> 00:17:11,405
and I'm quite eager to hear more
about the Yoh Kingdom.

366
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:12,823
We're grateful to you.

367
00:17:12,907 --> 00:17:15,785
[MAIKA] A feast!
We're gonna have a feast!

368
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:17,328
[Ars laughs] Oh, yes.

369
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:20,164
We'll make a big, delicious meal
in your honor.

370
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:21,582
[Takao grunts]

371
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:22,667
[Rietz grunts]

372
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,965
-[chatter continues]
-Is there a problem, Rietz?

373
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,091
Not sure.

374
00:17:30,925 --> 00:17:32,843
[RIETZ]
Is it just my imagination?

375
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:35,471
I can sense a faint smell
of blood.

376
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,098
-[swords clang]
-[grunts]

377
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,516
[both gasp]

378
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:41,560
[BANDIT] Oh, well,
that's not what should happen.

379
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:45,022
And here I was thinking
I'd found myself a blind spot.

380
00:17:45,106 --> 00:17:47,358
You must be
some kind of monster, huh?

381
00:17:49,277 --> 00:17:50,403
[Ars gasps]

382
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:52,905
Get back inside the room!

383
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,783
[gasps, grunts]

384
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,951
[running footsteps]

385
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:58,452
[grunts]

386
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:02,540
[screaming]

387
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,208
That's how
you handle 'em, Takao!

388
00:18:04,292 --> 00:18:05,501
Show 'em who's boss!

389
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:07,712
[grunting]

390
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,468
[grunting]

391
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,346
[BANDIT] Damn it!

392
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,640
[gasps]

393
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:25,313
[ARS] They were able
to stop an invisible attack?

394
00:18:25,396 --> 00:18:26,564
That's amazing!

395
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,483
The whole fight
was over in no time, too!

396
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,236
[MAIKA] Identify yourselves,
vermin!

397
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,697
So you're using
some kind of magic item.

398
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:35,990
That's your secret?

399
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:38,284
I've read about
some magical tools

400
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,369
that allow you
to hide in plain sight.

401
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:43,247
What's more, lately, there have
been a number of attacks

402
00:18:43,331 --> 00:18:46,042
reportedly carried out
by "invisible bandits."

403
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:49,211
Tell me, might you be
the perpetrators?

404
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:51,714
Bet you wish
you figured it out sooner.

405
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:52,715
[ARS] Rietz, help!

406
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:54,633
[all gasp]

407
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:56,510
[RIETZ] Lord Ars!

408
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,596
-Brother, no!
-[BANDIT] Not so fast.

409
00:18:58,679 --> 00:19:00,014
Stay right where you are.

410
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,724
Now, drop your weapons.

411
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:04,352
Just do what I tell you to,
and I might not kill him.

412
00:19:04,435 --> 00:19:06,354
[grunting]

413
00:19:13,027 --> 00:19:14,362
[bandit laughing]

414
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:17,740
I could tell this was nice
just by looking at it.

415
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,700
[BANDIT 2] Think we can get
some coin with it?

416
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:21,994
Yeah. It's kinda got
a weird shape,

417
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:23,913
but I'm sure
we can find a buyer soon.

418
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:25,748
Thing caught my eye
when I first saw 'em

419
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,167
walking around town with it.
[grunts]

420
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,087
Now that we got the sword,
what do we do with them?

421
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,880
Can't keep them
down here forever.

422
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:36,467
[BANDIT 1] Yohians are
pretty rare in these parts.

423
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:39,804
There's gotta be
a slaver around that'll buy 'em.

424
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,097
[ARS] Damn it.

425
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:43,557
These strangers came to Canarre
looking for help,

426
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:45,601
and now they're wrapped up
in our mess.

427
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,520
[BANDIT 1]
Hey, that one looks familiar.

428
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:50,231
I could swear
I've seen you before.

429
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:53,567
I can't imagine where,
because I'm just a--

430
00:19:53,651 --> 00:19:54,944
-[RIETZ] Merchant's son.
-Huh?

431
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:56,570
He's my master,
and I'm his slave.

432
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:58,989
-[laughter]
-What do you know about that?

433
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:02,076
He's gonna fetch us
a nice fat ransom, won't he?

434
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:04,703
Hey, bro, the boss wants to have
a quick word with you.

435
00:20:04,787 --> 00:20:06,664
[BANDIT 1]
Yeah, yeah, I'm coming.

436
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,332
[footsteps receding]

437
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:10,668
[Ars exhales]

438
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:15,756
[Ars sighs]

439
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,341
-[RIETZ] Lord Ars!
-Huh?

440
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:20,344
I'm on my hands and knees
begging for your forgiveness.

441
00:20:20,428 --> 00:20:22,138
As your most trusted retainer,

442
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,765
this kind of humiliating failure
is unforgivable.

443
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:27,059
I could never repay you
for such a massive blunder.

444
00:20:27,143 --> 00:20:30,020
Oh, no, it's all my fault
for letting my guard down.

445
00:20:30,104 --> 00:20:32,231
Please don't blame yourself
for what happened.

446
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:33,732
But I'm supposed to protect you.

447
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:35,609
-[gate clanks]
-Uh? Huh?

448
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:38,612
What are we going to do,
elder brother?

449
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,156
[Takao grunting]

450
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:47,496
What do you mean
they took Lord Ars away, huh?

451
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,457
You've got
some explaining to do.

452
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,916
You were supposed
to watch over him.

453
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,209
How could you let this happen?

454
00:20:52,293 --> 00:20:53,544
[GUARD] We were watching!

455
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:55,754
We had all of the entrances
and exits covered,

456
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:57,548
I swear to you.
But from out of nowhere,

457
00:20:57,631 --> 00:20:59,216
we were attacked
by an invisible enemy,

458
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:00,926
and there was nothing
we could do to stop them.

459
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:04,013
Did you say they were invisible?
Seriously?

460
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:06,640
-[GUARD] Yes, sir.
-Makes me wonder,

461
00:21:06,724 --> 00:21:08,267
is this related
to those bandit attacks?

462
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:09,977
[CHARLOTTE] It doesn't matter.
We've gotta go

463
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,604
and save them right now.
Where's Rosell?

464
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,522
[ZAHT] On a diplomatic mission
at the harbor.

465
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:16,650
[CHARLOTTE] Then who's gonna be
able to work us up a solid plan?

466
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:18,027
[JOE] We don't need one.

467
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,196
Let's just go bust some heads
and break him out.

468
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:23,282
Pardon. Hey, Lady Licia.
Are you feeling all right?

469
00:21:24,742 --> 00:21:26,410
[LICIA] Hey, Braham?

470
00:21:26,494 --> 00:21:28,287
I'll be dispatching
the elite unit

471
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:30,122
to the enemy base immediately.

472
00:21:30,206 --> 00:21:32,291
-I want you to lead them.
-Ma'am.

473
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:35,961
[LICIA] Zaht, go with him
and serve as vice-captain.

474
00:21:36,045 --> 00:21:37,671
Yeah, sure.

475
00:21:37,755 --> 00:21:40,049
[LICIA] I've been wanting
to deal with these pests,

476
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:41,967
and this is finally my chance.

477
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:44,053
And I swear on my very life,

478
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:47,515
if they harm one hair
on my dear Lord Ars' head,

479
00:21:48,599 --> 00:21:50,851
I'll track down
each one of their families

480
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:52,853
and slit their throats myself.

481
00:21:55,481 --> 00:21:59,026
[♪ closing theme song playing]

482
00:23:25,905 --> 00:23:28,073
[ZAHT]
Lady Licia is usually so sweet,

483
00:23:28,157 --> 00:23:30,492
but when she goes into
"protect Ars" mode, watch out.

484
00:23:30,576 --> 00:23:32,202
[CHARLOTTE] Well, yeah,
because she's a woman

485
00:23:32,286 --> 00:23:33,662
who loves her man.

486
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,789
[LICIA] Come on, you either need
to come up with a plan

487
00:23:35,873 --> 00:23:36,874
or shut up, you hear?

488
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:39,752
[CHARLOTTE]
Next time, "Off to Save Ars."

